With `--additional-axioms`, a precondition that calls a recursive predicate on a constructed value, such as `t.scoped(|s|)` for `t := Bin(op, Var(0), Var(1))` where `scoped` is `a.scoped(n) && b.scoped(n)` on `Bin`, is proved independently of the surrounding declarations: each separately checked conjunct of the inlined body now has the body's call permissions at its own fuel layer, an instance of the existing definition axiom (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/198). Before, the second conjunct was proved only when some unrelated term happened to unfold the first, so which of two equivalent declarations failed moved with declaration order. The option remains disabled by default.
